NNAAMMEE
       pam_wheel - Only permit root access to members of group wheel

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppaamm__wwhheeeell..ssoo [debug] [deny] [group=_n_a_m_e] [root_only] [trust]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The pam_wheel PAM module is used to enforce the so-called _w_h_e_e_l group.
       By default it permits access to the target user if the applicant user
       is a member of the _w_h_e_e_l group. If no group with this name exist, the
       module is using the group with the group-ID 00.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       ddeebbuugg
           Print debug information.

       ddeennyy
           Reverse the sense of the auth operation: if the user is trying to
           get UID 0 access and is a member of the wheel group (or the group
           of the ggrroouupp option), deny access. Conversely, if the user is not
           in the group, return PAM_IGNORE (unless ttrruusstt was also specified,
           in which case we return PAM_SUCCESS).

       ggrroouupp==_n_a_m_e
           Instead of checking the wheel or GID 0 groups, use the _n_a_m_e group
           to perform the authentication.

       rroooott__oonnllyy
           The check for wheel membership is done only when the target user
           UID is 0.

       ttrruusstt
           The pam_wheel module will return PAM_SUCCESS instead of PAM_IGNORE
           if the user is a member of the wheel group (thus with a little play
           stacking the modules the wheel members may be able to su to root
           without being prompted for a passwd).

MMOODDUULLEE TTYYPPEESS PPRROOVVIIDDEEDD
       The aauutthh and aaccccoouunntt module types are provided.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
       PAM_AUTH_ERR
           Authentication failure.

       PAM_BUF_ERR
           Memory buffer error.

       PAM_IGNORE
           The return value should be ignored by PAM dispatch.

       PAM_PERM_DENY
           Permission denied.

       PAM_SERVICE_ERR
           Cannot determine the user name.

       PAM_SUCCESS
           Success.

       PAM_USER_UNKNOWN
           User not known.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
       The root account gains access by default (rootok), only wheel members
       can become root (wheel) but Unix authenticate non-root applicants.

           su      auth     sufficient     pam_rootok.so
           su      auth     required       pam_wheel.so
           su      auth     required       pam_unix.so



